## The Belief

State the conviction plainly in one paragraph. No hedging, no caveats.
Write it so someone could argue against it. Describe what you believe
to be structurally true about markets, technology, or human behaviour —
not what you plan to build in response.

## Why This Could Be True

Two or three pieces of evidence or reasoning. Brief — this is not a proof.
Just enough to show the belief is grounded in something observable.

## What Would Change My Mind

Explicit falsification criteria. What evidence or event would cause you
to move this from HELD to QUESTIONING or ABANDONED?

This is the most important section. A thesis that cannot be falsified
is not a thesis — it is a preference. Being specific here is what
makes the thesis useful as a planning input.

